 ### Stop-the-pop
-Bounds the Gaussian response based on distance to the mean. Choose when using Gaussian splats. [1472-stop-the-pop](1472-stop-the-pop.md)
+A per-tile culling method that bounds the smallest quadratic distance from the tile to the Gaussian mean to estimate maximum per-pixel opacity [S1, unofficial]. It is designed for Gaussian splats where opacity decays smoothly from the mean, contrasting with LinPrim's chord-length approach [S1, unofficial]. Choose it when rendering Gaussian-based point clouds [1472-stop-the-pop](1472-stop-the-pop.md).
 
 ### XPR
-The extensible renderer framework that implements LinPrim. [XPR](52-xpr.md)
+An extensible cross-platform point-based differentiable renderer framework that implements LinPrim and other culling strategies [S1, unofficial]. It provides the rendering infrastructure and batched blending loops where LinPrim operates [S1, unofficial]. Choose it as the underlying renderer when using linear splats [52-xpr](52-xpr.md).
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity**: O(1) per primitive per tile, as it involves a constant number of slab pair checks (4) and a single comparison. [S1, unofficial]
-- **Memory Complexity**: O(1) auxiliary memory. [S1, unofficial]
-- **Strengths**: Simple to implement, no per-pixel checks needed, conservative culling. [S1, unofficial]
-- **Limitations**: The bound can be loose when the constraint attaining the maximum changes across the tile. [S1, unofficial]
-- **When to use**: When using linear splats with homogeneous density. [S1, unofficial]
